We introduce a novel method for strengthening digital circuits, which leverages SAT solvers to identify and intensify critical sections of the circuit. This approach commences by converting the original circuit into a gate-level representation using a standard tool like ABC, and subsequently applies our algorithm to this form. The algorithm's primary objective is to locate a subset of the circuit components that, when upgraded, enables the creation of a more compact and efficient design. To achieve this, we employ a SAT solver to identify a minimal set of gates that, when removed, would render the remaining circuit unfunctional. We then replace this minimal set with a more complex, optimized logic component, and integrate it back into the circuit. The algorithm iteratively repeats this process until no further enhancements are possible. Our method's efficacy is demonstrated through experiments conducted on a diverse set of benchmark circuits, which reveal that our algorithm can effectively strengthen digital circuits, yielding improved performance in terms of area, delay, and power consumption. The algorithm's source code is publicly available on the GitHub platform. The experimental results and associated benchmarks can be accessed at the specified URL. The experimental results and associated benchmarks can be accessed at the specified URL. \textit{https://github.com/abdelhamidkhaled/Circuit-Enhancement-Algorithm}.} 

